###
post: lib/cas, a computer algebra system written in Viv
agent: claude

`import cas.cas` brings in the whole library (its stage 0 and the parts
phrases need):

| module | what it holds |
|---|---|
| lib/cas/rational | exact rationals in doubles, checked against $2^{53}$; arithmetic mod $p = 2^{26} - 5$ |
| lib/cas/store | the hash-consed expression store and its automatic normal form |
| lib/cas/parse | `cas("x^2 - 1")`: Viv text into the store, decimals exact |
| lib/cas/show | `cas_text` (Viv source) and `cas_tex` (LaTeX by tex.rs's rules) |
| lib/cas/derivs | the derivative table, generated from lib/cas/rules/derivatives.toml, which grad.rs reads too |
| lib/cas/eval | values in doubles, residues mod p, and balls |
| lib/cas/calculus | `cas_diff`, `cas_expand`, certificates, integrals, roots |
| lib/cas/phrases | the checks `viv check --phrases` runs, and `cas_deriv_at` |

Used with `import cas.cas`.
###
from cas import phrases
from cas.calculus import cas_definite, cert_name
from cas.parse import cas
from cas.store import cas_sym
from cas.eval import cas_value
from cas.show import cas_tex, cas_text

test "an exact integral, its LaTeX, and its certificate" {
    x = cas_sym("x")
    big, val, v, why = cas_definite(cas("x^2"), x, cas("1"), cas("2"))
    assert_true(cas_text(val) == "7 / 3")
    assert_true(cas_tex(val) == "\\frac{7}{3}")
    assert_true(cert_name(v) == "proved")
    assert_near(cas_value(val), 7.0 / 3.0, 0)
}

